    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1600">

                <pb facs="1304" n="1188" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1188"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.77/83.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 190.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-10-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 16, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my despatch No. 185 of
                    October 10, on the subject of the Panamá-David railway, I have the honor to
                    report that the status of that matter remains the same as before the recent
                    special session of the National Assembly. Both bills passed by this Assembly
                    referring to the financing and construction of that railway have been vetoed by
                    the President.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. Whiting Andrews.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
